# F5 builds the program and runs it. What it prints goes in the panel, a line to a row,
# in place of what the compiler said, and the program's end is written under it. The
# status line says so too, and nothing is running afterwards.
# files hello.cm=class Main from IO\n  def main:\n    out("hello\\n")\n    out("again\\n")\n  end\nend\n
# open hello.cm
# args --catmintc @ROOT@/catmintc
# frames 4
# expect message hello finished
# expect status [hello finished]
# expect runner 0
# expect panel 1 3
# expect panelall hello|again|[finished]
1 key f5
2 wait idle
